   Backup / cloud-restore policy.
   See https://developer.android.com/about/versions/12/backup-restore

   This app stores end-user PII locally:
   - chat history & roleplay state in Room (selfgemma_talk.db)
   - personas / cutouts / settings / skills in DataStore proto files
     (selfgemma_talk_*.pb under files/datastore)
   - cloud-LLM API keys in EncryptedSharedPreferences
     (selfgemma_talk_cloud_credentials)
   - HuggingFace OAuth state in AppAuth shared prefs
   - downloaded model weights and persona/role media under files/ and
     externalFiles/

   None of the above should leave the device via Google Cloud Backup. The
   policy below explicitly excludes every storage domain by listing root
   excludes; nothing is whitelisted for cloud-backup. Device-to-device
   transfer (during phone migration) is also denied because the encrypted
   credentials and Room database are not portable across installs without
   coordinated migration logic.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
